; `show` is not a name any more (0.7.4), and this is the fixture that
; keeps it that way.
;
; It was the head every `{hole}` and every `(println x)` lowered to,
; so a program could call it - and could also DECLARE it, and capture
; the lowering (tests/selfhost/383-format-capture.ax). The lowering
; emits `format#` now, which `#` makes unwritable, and `(format x)` is
; the only spelling. So `(show 1)` has to be the ordinary
; undefined-variable error and nothing special at all.
;
; `Fmt` and `Str` are loaded, which is what the rewrite targets, so
; nothing here is missing but the name: this file would compile if the
; name still existed.
;
; WHY THIS IS NOT VACUOUS. Reverting `showIsHead` in
; self_host/typecheck.ax to `(strEq (bareOf hname) "show")` and
; `expFmtShow` in self_host/expand.ax to `(expFmtCall env "show" ...)`
; makes the call resolve again - `checkVar`'s quiet arm suppresses the
; AX3001 for a `show` HEAD - and this golden's only line disappears.
(import Fmt)

(import Str)

(:: main Int)

(fn (main) (strLen (show 1)))
